      "gap": "The routed definition (body lines 15-35) defines uniform integrability only for families of integrable variables, whereas Durrett's definition (p. 244) applies to any collection of random variables, with integrability of every member a consequence (his remark sup E|X_i| <= M+1). The routed text does not state Durrett's arbitrary-collection form or prove that it agrees with the handbook definition. That source variant is written only in the unrouted owner file handbook/parts/p15/limit-theorems-and-concentration-w02c-p15-014.tex lines 563-597 (owner packet w02c-p15-014).",
