        }
      ],
      "gap": "The routed criterion requires Phi finite and Borel measurable and applies to families already assumed integrable. Durrett's Theorem 4.6.2 (p. 245) takes any function phi >= 0 with phi(x)/x -> infinity, assumes no integrability, and proves the bound with eps_M = sup{x/phi(x): x >= M}. The routed text does not preserve that source form (integrability derived from the moment bound, the explicit eps_M bound) and gives no worked boundary for the criterion (failure for phi(x)=x, need for a uniform bound, sufficiency without necessity for a fixed phi). These are written only in the unrouted owner file handbook/parts/p15/limit-theorems-and-concentration-w02c-p15-014.tex lines 599-672 (owner packet w02c-p15-014).",
